        {
          "id": "source-line-representation-disagrees-with-comment-coordinates",
          "severity": "medium",
          "impact": "A valid saved comment can silently acquire a quotation from a different physical line, or expected-quote verification rejects its correct source. Exact mapped follow-up comments can likewise be stored on the wrong LF-delimited line.",
          "locations": [
            {
              "side": "head",
              "path": "src/structure/parse.mjs",
              "contains": "  for (const match of source.matchAll(/\\r\\n|\\r|\\n/g)) {"
            }
          ],
          "witnesses": [
            {
              "input": {
                "body": "Header\rSubheading\nTarget\n",
                "commentLine": 2,
                "action": "capture anchor from the public comment without expectedQuote"
              },
              "expected": {
                "quote": "Target\n",
                "start": 18,
                "end": 25,
                "commentLine": 2
              },
              "actual": {
                "quote": "Subheading\n",
                "start": 7,
                "end": 18,
                "commentLine": 2
              }
            }
          ],
          "rubric": "One representation-contract defect recognizes lone CR as an extra structure line while unchanged persisted comments use LF-delimited physical coordinates. The meaningful regression is a reachable wrong quotation, rejected correct quotation, misplaced follow-up comment, or independently supported equivalent public consequence. A complete shorter or different witness receives full credit; no private body string, second symptom, follow-up route, file set, read count or tool route is required. A changed parser line count alone does not establish the asserted public comment-contract harm. Static proof is admissible. Review the actual active unchanged producer/consumer contract when adjudicating the claim, without requiring a canonical evidence path. Do not count the related capture and follow-up symptoms as separate defects. Independently review any genuine additional finding for all conditions."
        }
      ],
